<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring basis steady.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring basis steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids for dark northern spring wheat were mostly lower in line with a decline in MGE futures while basis levels remained broadly steady in thin trade, grain dealers in the northern U.S. grain belt said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>MGE Dec spring wheat closed down 3-1/4 cents at $4.01-3/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>One Montana dealer said farmer sales remained very slow while movement of previously contracted supplies had also ground to a virtual halt as snow swept into the state.</p>
<p>White wheat prices, however, were slightly higher.  </p>
